{"name":"Curious","hex":"#d9e49e","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"curious","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Tending to ask questions, or to want to explore or investigate; inquisitive;  nosy, prying.","Caused by curiosity."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Containing or pertaining to trivalent curium."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/curious"}],"entries":[{"title":"Curious (Hayley Kiyoko song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Curious\" is a song by American singer-songwriter Hayley Kiyoko, from her debut studio album Expectations (2018). It was released as the album's third single on January 11, 2018 by Empire/Atlantic Records. Kiyoko co-wrote \"Curious\" with Lisa Vitale, Brandon Colbein, Jakob Hazell and Svante Halldin, while Jack & Coke produced the song. The dance-pop, R&B and synth-pop track details Kiyoko confronting an ex-girlfriend she believes is dating a man to mask her true feelings for Kiyoko. Its title adopts \"curious\", a term used within the LGBT community to express casual same-sex experimentation, as Kiyoko demands the truth about the authenticity of her love interest's new relationship."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Curious_(Hayley_Kiyoko_song)","wikidata":"Q85754835"},{"title":"Curiosity","blocks":[{"text":"Curiosity can be a quality related to inquisitive thinking, such as exploration, investigation, and learning, evident in humans and other animals. It can also refer to something which can cause curiosity. When it is for an object it may be called a curio, and a collection of curios or curiosities may be stored together as a collection called curiosities."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/60/Kom%C3%A9ta_C-2020_F3_%28NEOWISE%29.jpg/330px-Kom%C3%A9ta_C-2020_F3_%28NEOWISE%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Curiosity","wikidata":"Q366791"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.w